# rust-analyzer starts a `rustc` to discover the sysroot and exits on `exit` without waiting for or stopping it.
# L9 passes when that rustc ends within lspcheck's one-second grace after the server and fails when it doesn't;
# both verdicts are right for what lspcheck saw. Discovery took 0.8 s on one CI runner and 4.2 s on another
# (2026-11-09), and a rustc slowed to 4 s locally fails L9 in every scenario.
